{
    "background_story": "Eliel was a renowned herbalist in a small village nestled in the rolling hills of medieval England. He spent most of his days tending to the local flora, studying the properties of each plant, and experimenting with new remedies. Among his prized possessions was a rare and precious batch of agueweed, a plant rumored to cure even the most stubborn fevers. Eliel's fascination with agueweed began when his own mother was cured of a deadly illness by a local healer who used the plant in her treatment. Since then, he dedicated himself to mastering the art of cultivating and preparing agueweed, using it to heal countless villagers afflicted by malaria and other diseases. Eliel's expertise and generosity earned him the respect and gratitude of the community, who came to rely on him as their guardian of health and wellness.",
